<article class="env-lemma" id="017T">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/017T">Lemma <span data-tag="017T">14.18.4</span>.</a> Let $U$ be a simplicial set. Let $n \geq 0$ be an integer. The rule </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  U'_ m = \bigcup \nolimits _{\varphi : [m] \to [i], \  i\leq n} \mathop{\mathrm{Im}}(U(\varphi ))  \]
</div>
  <p> defines a sub simplicial set $U' \subset U$ with $U'_ i = U_ i$ for $i \leq n$. Moreover, all $m$-simplices of $U'$ are degenerate for all $m > n$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      If $x \in U_ m$ and $x = U(\varphi )(y)$ for some $y \in U_ i$, $i \leq n$ and some $\varphi : [m] \to [i]$ then any image $U(\psi )(x)$ for any $\psi : [m'] \to [m]$ is equal to $U(\varphi \circ \psi )(y)$ and $\varphi \circ \psi : [m'] \to [i]$. Hence $U'$ is a simplicial set. By construction all simplices in dimension $n + 1$ and higher are degenerate. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>